    "reason": "[ev-d1948f134793] says only that the TCP LoadBalancer `terminationDelay` option \"has been removed\" and can now be set on `TCPServersTransport`. It does not say what happens to configurations that still set it: whether the value is ignored, rejected or still honoured. The deterministic check also found that `IngressRouteTCP` `spec.routes[].services[].terminationDelay` is still in the v3.0.0 schema [ev-f7d1f0ce407c], so the claim that the field \"will be ignored\" is not supported. Deciding between setting-ignored, resource-rejected and deprecation needs upstream text or code showing how v3.0.0 handles the field when it is set.",
